# 1. CASE Expression

The `CASE` expression works like an **IF-ELSE statement** in programming languages.

## Syntax

```sql
CASE
    WHEN condition THEN value
    WHEN condition THEN value
    ELSE value
END
```

---

## Example 1: Customer Membership

Classify customers according to their points.

```sql
SELECT
    customer_id,
    first_name,
    last_name,
    points,
    CASE
        WHEN points < 1000 THEN 'Bronze'
        WHEN points BETWEEN 1000 AND 2000 THEN 'Silver'
        WHEN points BETWEEN 2001 AND 3000 THEN 'Gold'
        ELSE 'Platinum'
    END AS membership
FROM customers;
```

### Output

|Customer|Points|Membership|
|---------|------|----------|
|John|850|Bronze|
|Mary|1700|Silver|
|Alex|2500|Gold|
|Emma|3500|Platinum|

---

## Example 2: Order Status

```sql
SELECT
    order_id,
    status,
    CASE
        WHEN status = 1 THEN 'Pending'
        WHEN status = 2 THEN 'Shipped'
        WHEN status = 3 THEN 'Delivered'
        ELSE 'Unknown'
    END AS order_status
FROM orders;
```

